# Copy to build.config (git-ignored) and fill in. make (app/scripts/config.sh) reads it and writes the Xcode settings
# into app/Platforms/macOS/Config/Local.xcconfig; a variable set in the environment wins over the file. Lines are NAME=value; quotes are optional.

# Apple Developer Team ID (Apple Developer → Membership details). iCloud needs a paid team, not a Personal Team.
CEVICHE_TEAM_ID=
# The app's bundle identifier; Xcode registers it on the first build with CEVICHE_ICLOUD=1.
CEVICHE_BUNDLE_ID=me.chichou.ceviche
# CloudKit and iCloud Drive container. Defaults to iCloud.<bundle ID>.
#CEVICHE_ICLOUD_CONTAINER=iCloud.me.chichou.ceviche
# Signing certificate: its name, or its SHA-1 hash from `security find-identity -v -p codesigning` when several share a
# name. Unset: Xcode signs for the team when iCloud is on, otherwise the build is signed ad hoc.
#CEVICHE_SIGN_IDENTITY=
# With CEVICHE_SIGN_IDENTITY and iCloud on: the installed provisioning profile to sign with, by name or UUID.
#CEVICHE_PROVISIONING_PROFILE=
# make snapshot notarizes with this notarytool keychain profile (xcrun notarytool store-credentials <name>), signing
# with the team's Developer ID Application identity unless CEVICHE_SIGN_IDENTITY says otherwise.
#CEVICHE_NOTARY_PROFILE=
# iCloud catalogs and iCloud Drive: 1 turns them on (Xcode then signs for CEVICHE_TEAM_ID, with the Apple Developer
# account signed in to Xcode), 0 (the default) leaves them out.
#CEVICHE_ICLOUD=0
# Where a build without iCloud Drive keeps LUTs and profiles: folders or database.
#CEVICHE_LOCAL_STORAGE=folders
# Which build to make. community (the default): open source, macOS 15+, no store or badge, and models installed by hand
# from the release page. appstore: the Mac App Store build, macOS 26+, with Ceviche Pro and models delivered by the
# App Store.
#CEVICHE_DISTRIBUTION=community
# App Sandbox: 1 or 0. On by default only for the App Store build, which needs it.
#CEVICHE_SANDBOX=0
# iOS and iPadOS: 1 also builds the export codecs for iOS and the iOS Simulator (about 40 s more, once), which iOS
# builds of the package then link. 0 (the default) builds them for macOS only.
#CEVICHE_IOS=0
# Ceviche Pro, the App Store build's one-time purchase that removes the Unpaid badge: its product ID from App Store
# Connect (comma-separated if there are several). Only IDs go here. App Store Connect API keys and the shared secret are
# never needed by the app; keep them out of this file and the repository.
#CEVICHE_STORE_PRODUCTS=
